  "response": "<think>\nWe need to find the smallest positive integer n satisfying:\n\nn ≡ 2 (mod 5)\nn ≡ 3 (mod 7)\nn ≡ 4 (mod 9)\n\nWe can solve using Chinese remainder theorem. Since moduli are pairwise coprime? 5,7,9: gcd(5,7)=1, gcd(5,9)=1, gcd(7,9)=1? Actually 7 and 9 are coprime (gcd=1). So they are pairwise coprime. So there is a unique solution modulo product = 5*7*9 = 315.\n\nWe can find n.\n\nLet's solve:\n\nn ≡ 2 mod 5 => n = 5a + 2.\n\nPlug into second: 5a + 2 ≡ 3 (mod 7) => 5a ≡ 1 (mod 7). Compute inverse of 5 mod 7. 5*3=15≡1 mod7, so inverse is 3. So a ≡ 3*1 = 3 (mod 7). So a = 7b + 3.\n\nThus n = 5(7b+3) + 2 = 35b + 15 + 2 = 35b + 17.\n\nNow satisfy third: n ≡ 4 mod 9 => 35b + 17 ≡ 4 (mod 9). Compute 35 mod 9: 9*3=27, remainder 8. So 35 ≡ 8 (mod 9). Also 17 mod 9 = 8 (since 9*1=9, remainder 8). So equation: 8b + 8 ≡ 4 (mod 9) => 8b ≡ -4 ≡ 5 (mod 9) because 8b+8 ≡4 => subtract 8 both sides: 8b ≡ 4-8 = -4 ≡ 5 mod9. So 8b ≡ 5 (mod 9). Inverse of 8 mod 9? Since gcd(8,9)=1, inverse is number x such that 8x ≡1 mod9. 8*8=64≡1 mod9 because 63 is multiple, remainder 1. So inverse is 8. Multiply both sides by 8: b ≡ 8*5 = 40 ≡ 40 mod9 => 9*4=36, remainder 4. So b ≡ 4 (mod 9). So b = 9c + 4.\n\nThus n = 35(9c+4) + 17 = 315c + 140 + 17 = 315c + 157.\n\nSmallest positive integer is when c=0 => n = 157. Check: 157 mod5 = 2? 5*31=155, remainder 2 yes. 157 mod7 =? 7*22=154, remainder 3 yes. 157 mod9 =? 9*17=153, remainder 4 yes. So answer is 157.\n\nThus output JSON {n:157}. The instruction: \"只输出 JSON {n}.\" So we need to output exactly:\n\n{\n  \"n\": 157\n}\n\nProbably with no extra text. Ensure proper JSON formatting. Let's produce that.\n</think>\n{\n  \"n\": 157\n}",
